@startuml services-classes-after
' Services / API data-access classes on team/relay after Relay's A4 tickets
' MRD-166, MRD-247 and MRD-77 (Java half). Compare services-classes-before.puml.
' Reverse-engineered from services/src/ca/meridian on origin/team/relay (Nov 21, 2026).
' Green = new, yellow = changed, grey = outside the services code, white = unchanged context.
!pragma layout smetana
title Services data access: AFTER (team/relay, MRD-166 + MRD-247 + MRD-77)
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor<<new>> #D5F0D5
  BackgroundColor<<changed>> #FFF3C4
  BackgroundColor<<external>> #EEEEEE
  BackgroundColor<<context>> #FFFFFF
}

package "ca.meridian.api" {
  class ForecastHandler <<changed>> {
    -db : Db
    +handle(ex)
    ~parseQuery(raw) : Map
  }
  class SeriesHandler <<changed>> {
    -db : Db
    +handle(ex)
  }
  class ForecastV2 <<context>> {
    -db : DbClient
    -cache : ForecastCache
  }
}

package "ca.meridian.admin" {
  class AdminCli <<context>> {
    ~evict(station, year)
  }
}

package "ca.meridian.db" {
  class Db <<changed>> {
    -dbPath : String
    +path() : String
    +queryJson(sql) : String
    +queryJson(sql, params : Object...) : String
    -open() : Connection
    -resultCode(e) : int
    -asTheProgramPrintedIt(rows, store) : String
  }
  class DbClient <<context>> {
    -db : Db
    -retries : int
    +raw() : Db
    +query(sql) : ResultSetLite
    +queryJson(sql) : String
    -isTransient(e) : boolean
  }
  class ForecastCache <<changed>> {
    -db : DbClient
    -ttlMillis : long
    -marks : EvictionMarks
    -entries : ConcurrentHashMap<String, Entry>
    +summary(station) : Summary
    +invalidate(station, year)
    +clear()
    +size() : int
    -load(station) : Summary
    -key(station) : String
  }
  class EvictionMarks <<new>> {
    ~{static} UNKNOWN : String
    ~{static} NONE : String
    -dir : Path
    ~token(station) : String
    ~mark(station)
    ~{static} isUnknown(token) : boolean
  }
  class QueryBuilder <<context>>
}

class "SQLite JDBC driver 3.46.1.3\nservices/lib/sqlite-jdbc-3.46.1.3.jar\n(runs inside the service's JVM)" as Driver <<external>>
class "<store path>.evict/<station>\none small note file per station" as Notes <<external>>

ForecastHandler --> Db : queryJson(sql, bound values)
SeriesHandler --> Db : queryJson(sql, bound values)
ForecastV2 --> DbClient
ForecastV2 --> ForecastCache
AdminCli --> DbClient
AdminCli ..> ForecastCache : creates its own
DbClient --> Db
ForecastCache --> DbClient
ForecastCache ..> QueryBuilder
ForecastCache *-- EvictionMarks : one per cache
EvictionMarks ..> Notes : reads (server), writes (admin tool)
Db ..> Driver : DriverManager.getConnection("jdbc:sqlite:" + path)

note right of ForecastHandler
  MRD-166: the station (and the year on /api/series)
  is bound to ?1 / ?2, never written into the SQL.
  Responses are meant to be byte-identical to before.
end note

note bottom of ForecastCache
  MRD-247: one entry per station, key(station) for
  reads and evictions alike (the notes folder is found
  through db.raw().path()). Each entry remembers the
  eviction token it was loaded under. invalidate() now
  throws IOException if the note cannot be written.
end note

note right of Db
  MRD-77: no sqlite3 program. The error text is still
  "sqlite3 exited N", with N = SQLite's result code,
  because DbClient.isTransient() matches "exited 5".
  queryColumn() is gone; nothing called it.
end note

note bottom of EvictionMarks
  Package-private. Only valid station ids become file names.
  Any trouble reading a note gives UNKNOWN, which makes
  the cache load fresh and never cache.
end note
@enduml
